ndependent closures over the single league string; none share mutable state. The dict is ready to be spread into a module namespace via globals().update(...). Parameters Returns Keys are the public function names (e.g. \"ahl_schedule\").","s":"build_family","u":"/docs/gojhl/reference/additional","h":"#build_family","p":12369},{"i":12375,"t":"gojhl_game_corsi(game_id: 'int', return_as_pandas: 'bool' = False) -> 'Any' Player-level on-ice Corsi and Fenwick for a single GOJHL game. Parameters Returns One row per player on ice for a shot attempt: player_id (String), corsi_for / corsi_against / corsi_for_pct, fenwick_for / fenwick_against / fenwick_for_pct, corsi_includes_missed (Boolean), toi_seconds (Int64) and corsi_for_per60 (Float64, null without time on ice). A pandas DataFrame when return_as_pandas is True. Raises","s":"gojhl_game_corsi","u":"/docs/gojhl/reference/additional","h":"#gojhl_game_corsi","p":12369},{"i":12377,"t":"gojhl_game_shifts(game_id: 'int', return_as_pandas: 'bool' = False) -> 'Any' Parsed shift stints for a single GOJHL game. Parameters Returns One row per shift: game_id and player_id (Int64), first_name, last_name, jersey_number, home (Int64, 1 = home), period, start_time / end_time / length (clock strings), start_s / end_s (Int64 seconds) and the goal_on_shift / penalty_on_shift flags. A pandas DataFrame when return_as_pandas is True. Raises","s":"gojhl_game_shifts","u":"/docs/gojhl/reference/additional","h":"#gojhl_game_shifts","p":12369},{"i":12379,"t":"gojhl_game_summary(game_id: 'int') -> 'dict' GOJHL game summary — dict of frames (game/goals/penalties/shots_by_period/three_stars). Parameters Returns game (one row: game_id, date, status, venue, attendance, both teams and scores), goals (one row per goal with the scorer, both assists and the plus / minus skaters), penalties (one row per penalty), shots_by_period (side, period, shots) and three_stars. When the league denies the summary view, the event frames are empty and game is a game_id stub row. Raises","s":"gojhl_game_summary","u":"/docs/gojhl/reference/additional","h":"#gojhl_game_summary","p":12369},{"i":12381,"t":"gojhl_leaders(season: 'Optional[int]' = None, season_id: 'Optional[int]' = None, return_as_pandas: 'bool' = False) -> 'Any' GOJHL statistical leaders for a given season. Parameters Returns One row per ranked skater (points and goals leaders): rank (Int64), player_id, name, jersey_number, position, team_id / team_name / team_code, stat_formatted and type_formatted (String), plus photo and logo URLs. A pandas DataFrame when return_as_pandas is True. Raises","s":"gojhl_leaders","u":"/docs/gojhl/reference/additional","h":"#gojhl_leaders","p":12369},{"i":12383,"t":"gojhl_pbp(game_id: 'int', return_as_pandas: 'bool' = False) -> 'Any' GOJHL play-by-play — one row per event, fully enriched. Parameters Returns One row per event (shot, goal, penalty, faceoff, hit, goalie change ...): game_id, event, team_id, period_of_game, time_of_period, rink x_coord / y_coord (Float64, raw 600×300 coordinates), the primary / second / third player and goalie ids and names, the plus / minus skaters on a goal, game metadata from the game summary, and derived shot_distance / shot_angle / scoring_chance and the on_ice_home / on_ice_away skaters from the shift feed. Player ids are Float64 here. Some leagues (USHL, MJHL) publish only goals, penalties and goalie changes, with no coordinates. A pandas DataFrame when return_as_pandas is True. Raises","s":"gojhl_pbp","u":"/docs/gojhl/reference/additional","h":"#gojhl_pbp","p":12369},{"i":12385,"t":"gojhl_player_stats(player_id: 'int', return_as_pandas: 'bool' = False) -> 'Any' GOJHL player season stats across all seasons. Parameters Returns One row per season (and team) the player played: season_id, season_name, playoff, team_id / team_name / team_code, games_played, goals, assists, points, plus_minus, penalty_minutes, power-play / short-handed / shootout splits, shots, faceoff_wins / faceoff_attempts, ice_time and stat_type (String, as the feed ships them). A pandas DataFrame when return_as_pandas is True. Raises","s":"gojhl_player_stats","u":"/docs/gojhl/reference/additional","h":"#gojhl_player_stats","p":12369},{"i":12387,"t":"gojhl_player_toi(game_id: 'int', return_as_pandas: 'bool' = False) -> 'Any' Per-player time-on-ice totals for a single GOJHL game. Parameters Returns One row per player: player_id (Int64), first_name, last_name, toi_seconds (Int64), num_shifts and avg_shift_s (Float64). A pandas DataFrame when return_as_pandas is True. Raises","s":"gojhl_player_toi","u":"/docs/gojhl/reference/additional","h":"#gojhl_player_toi","p":12369},{"i":12389,"t":"gojhl_schedule(season: 'Optional[int]' = None, season_id: 'Optional[int]' = None, return_as_pandas: 'bool' = False) -> 'Any' GOJHL schedule — one row per game of one season. Parameters Returns One row per game: game_id, game_date, game_status, home_team / home_team_id / home_score, away_team / away_team_id / away_score, venue, season_id and game_type (all String). Only the requested season's games: a regular season, its playoffs and its preseason are separate season ids, so pass season_id (from gojhl_season_id()) for the playoffs. A pandas DataFrame when return_as_pandas is True. Raises","s":"gojhl_schedule","u":"/docs/gojhl/reference/additional","h":"#gojhl_schedule","p":12369},{"i":12391,"t":"gojhl_standings(season: 'Optional[int]' = None, season_id: 'Optional[int]' = None, return_as_pandas: 'bool' = False) -> 'Any' GOJHL standings — one row per team. Parameters Returns One row per team: team, team_code, team_rank and wins (Int64), and games_played, losses, regulation_wins, non_reg_wins, non_reg_losses, points, goals_for, goals_against, games_remaining, percentage and overall_rank (String, as the feed ships them). A pandas DataFrame when return_as_pandas is True. Raises","s":"gojhl_standings","u":"/docs/gojhl/reference/additional","h":"#gojhl_standings","p":12369},{"i":12393,"t":"gojhl_team_roster(team_id: 'int', season: 'Optional[int]' = None, season_id: 'Optional[int]' = None, return_as_pandas: 'bool' = False) -> 'Any' GOJHL team roster for a given team + season. Parameters Returns One row per rostered player: player_id, person_id, names (first_name, last_name, display_name), position, tp_jersey_number, shoots / catches, height / weight, birthdate, home and birth places, rookie, veteran_status, draft_status and player_image (String, as the feed ships them). A pandas DataFrame when return_as_pandas is True. Raises","s":"gojhl_team_roster","u":"/docs/gojhl/reference/additional","h":"#gojhl_team_roster","p":12369},{"i":12395,"t":"gojhl_teams(season: 'Optional[int]' = None, season_id: 'Optional[int]' = None, return_as_pandas: 'bool' = False) -> 'Any' GOJHL teams for a given season. Parameters Returns One row per team: team_id, team_name, team_code, team_nickname, team_label, division and team_logo (String). A pandas DataFrame when return_as_pandas is True. Raises","s":"gojhl_teams","u":"/docs/gojhl/reference/additional","h":"#gojhl_teams","p":12369},{"i":12398,"t":"gojhl_season_id(return_as_pandas: 'bool' = False) -> 'Any' All GOJHL seasons with end-year + game-type labels. Parameters Returns One row per season: season_id (Int64), season_name, season_short, career, playoff, start_date, end_date, season_yr (Int64, the END year) and game_type_label. A pandas DataFrame when return_as_pandas is True. Raises","s":"gojhl_season_id","u":"/docs/gojhl/reference/additional","h":"#gojhl_season_id","p":12369},{"i":12400,"t":"most_recent_gojhl_season() -> 'int' Newest GOJHL regular season as an end-year integer: the highest season_yr of a regular season that is not a one-off event, so a preseason listed first is not a default. Returns The newest regular season's END year (2026 = the 2025-26 season). Raises","s":"most_recent_gojhl_season","u":"/docs/gojhl/reference/additional","h":"#most_recent_gojhl_season","p":12369}],"index":{"version":"2.3.9","fields":["t"],"fieldVectors":[["t/12366",[0,3.23